MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_001: Harmph, mmph, mmm. Ahhh! That hits the spot!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_002: Oh my. So much mead and dried meat.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_003: Huh? Hey, I know you. You're Ulta!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_004: It's Ultand.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_005: Tobias, has anyone ever told you to take better care\nof your health?
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_006: Hehehe. Relax. Mead and meat have been my bread\nand butter for years.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_007: That and wine! A little every day'll keep you in the\npink of health.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_008: Please tell me this isn't what you eat every day.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_009: You bet it is. Ever since I was young.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_010: I always knock back a few after a long day's work.\nIt's the life, I tell you! Hehehe!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_011: You keep this up, and you'll destroy yourself.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_012: Hehehe! I'm made of stronger stuff than that. There's\nnot a weak bone in my body!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_013: Oh, really? You know, you're about the same age as\nmy father.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_014: No kidding? Well, come to think of it...I guess I don't\nget outta bed as easy as I used to.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_015: A crack in the armor. A little thing like that can be\nan indicator of a serious illness.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_016: Especially if you don't change the way you eat...\nOh! I've got an idea!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_017: I'll show you what a healthy meal looks like.\nStay here!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_018: Hey, this oughta be good. Betcha that Ulta would\nmake someone a fine wife.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_019: Yeah...huh. "Someone."
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_020: Maybe she'll be the one to hang the "SOLD" sign on\nmy independent livin'.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_021: Here you go! It's nothing fancy, but I'm sure you'll\nlove it.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_022: Huh? What is this stuff?
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_023: Looks like...little sticky things, steamed\nwith couscous.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_024: It's tenebato. Nutrient-rich fermented beans.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_025: Just the thing for anyone who's had too much mead.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_026: This sticky stuff's supposed to be a hangover cure?\nSmells nasty enough to wake the dead!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_027: It's supposed to be like that. It's our family recipe,\ntenebato couscous. Eat up!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_028: How? I just don't... I can't eat this, OK?
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_029: What are you, some kind of picky baby?
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_030: Gimme a break! I'm outta here.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_C_031: You get back here and finish your meal, mister!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_001: Oh. Hello, Tobias. How are you?
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_002: Oh! Ulta! Still healthy as a horse. So no need for a\nsecond helping of the sticky stuff.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_003: Ultand. I see you're stuffing your face with mead and\nmeat again.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_004: I have heard that mead can offer some healthful\nbenefits...in small quantities.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_005: But I still think your diet is atrocious.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_006: You didn't finish the other day, did you?\nMy delicious tenebato?
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_007: I can stomach basically anything. Except for\nthose beans.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_008: Well, it's your lucky day. I've been researching a\ndiversity of tenebato cuisine.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_009: If you think you're gonna get me to choke down that\nsticky slime...
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_010: I'm not taking no for an answer. You have to try\nwhat I prepare.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_011: The Lionheart of Saramis isn't going to run away like\na scared little boy again, is he?
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_012: Nnnngh.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_013: First up! Roasted, marinaded tenebato seafood!\nI, um, used some spices to mask the smell.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_014: You just made sticky fish.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_015: Not into it? OK, next up is...tenebato meat soup!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_016: Soup is a nice, smooth slurp...right?
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_017: Ugh! I can feel those stringy bits going down. Gross.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_018: Not a favorite? Well, try this, then.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_019: Whoa... Dagdan stick bugs in sweet-and-sour sauce!\nWe love this stuff in Saramis.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_020: I mean, you went and put those beans in it, but eh.\nWhere'd you find out about this dish?
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_021: I did some reading on Saramis cuisine in the\ntemple records.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_022: I'd never cooked with bugs before, but I caught some,\nand here you go!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_023: Well...if you went to all the trouble, I better hold my\nnose and dig in.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_024: Ughh... Rrrgh... Ungh... Hang on a sec...
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_025: Now this I can do!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_026: The gooeyness goes good with the sweet-and-sour\nsauce. Plus it's got that stick-bug crunch to it!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_027: Really?! You like it?!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_028: Baw haw haw! Do your worst, gooey gunk! The\nLionheart of Saramis's stomach is undefeated!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_029: Hehe. Hey, no need to eat so fast. Slow down\na little.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_030: Y'know what would be nice with a strong taste\nlike this? Some mead!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_031: More mead? The whole point is to change your diet\nand take care of yourself!
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_032: Well, what do you know? I cleaned my plate.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_033: Thanks, Ulta. Good stuff! And with that, I oughta\nbe going.
MID_SE_Hur_Tob_B_034: Wait! Come back!